# Lesson 2, new hand: open 1NT with 15, partner invites, decline.
title: Partner invites: decline with 15
id: L02-14
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.4, 2.7
student: S
board: 14
dealer: E
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  Q84    J73    KJT    QT95
  E  9762   A5     A85    J862
  S  AJ5    KQ8    Q962   K73
  W  KT3    T9642  743    A4

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1NT*   = 15-17 points, balanced
     key: 15 HCP and balanced: open 1NT.
     not 1D: Did you count 15? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT.
     not *: Did you count 15? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT.
  W Pass
  N 2NT    = 8-9 points, balanced: an invitation
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = A minimum: decline
     key: Partner asks you to bid game with the top of your range. 15 is the bottom, so pass.
     not 3NT: 2NT is an invitation. Are you at the top of your 15-17 range?
     not *: Partner asks you to bid game with the top of your range. Are you at the top?
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2NT invited game: bid 3NT with a maximum, pass with a minimum.
  15 is the bottom of your range, so your side may have only 23. You
  decline. You are declarer, because you bid no-trump first, and so West
  will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W H4  N H3  E HA  S H8
  2   E H5  S HQ  W H2  N H7
  3   S D2  W D3  N DK  E DA
      note: The plan: drive out the ♦A for three diamond tricks, and take two tricks each in hearts and clubs.
  4   E S2  S S5  W SK  N S4
  5   W H6  N HJ  E S6  S HK
  6   S D6  W D4  N DJ  E D5
      note: Now your diamond winners: over to dummy's ♦J.
  7   N DT  E D8  S DQ  W D7
      note: Back to your ♦Q.
  8   S D9  W S3  N C5  E S7
      note: Your last diamond is a winner.
  9   S C3  W C4  N CQ  E C2
      note: A club to dummy's ♣Q.
  10  N C9  E C6  S C7  W CA
      note: Lead a club from dummy. West's ace takes it.
  11  W HT  N CT  E S9  S SJ
  12  W H9  N S8  E C8  S SA
  13  W ST  N SQ  E CJ  S CK
      note: 7 tricks: 2NT down one.

play recap:
  The plan: drive out the ♦A for three diamond tricks, and take two tricks
  each in hearts and clubs.

  2NT down one. The defenders took their aces, the ♠K and West's long
  hearts. Good defense beat a sound contract, and that's a normal result.
  With 15 opposite partner's 8-9, your side had 24, and passing the
  invitation was right.
